Notolog source-package layout
=============================

This is a binary-repack source package. It retains the upstream source under
src/ and includes the architecture-specific PyInstaller executable at
pyinstaller/dist/notolog. debian/rules validates and installs that executable;
the executable is not rebuilt by the Debian package build.

Preparing and rebuilding
------------------------

On an Ubuntu 22.04 amd64 build host, install the packages listed in
debian/control plus Python 3.14, zlib1g-dev, libegl1, libportaudio2, devscripts,
and lintian. From a clean builder checkout, populate src/ from the upstream
release matching debian/changelog:

    git clone --depth 1 --branch v1.2.3 \
        https://github.com/notolog/notolog-editor.git src
    TARGET_SERIES_OVERRIDE=jammy ./pyinstaller/build.sh

The script builds and audits the executable, creates the binary package, and
runs frozen-module and headless smoke tests. To create an unsigned source
package afterward, run:

    dpkg-buildpackage -S -sa -us -uc

Modifying or discarding changes
-------------------------------

Make executable changes in src/ or the PyInstaller configuration, then rerun
the commands above. Do not edit pyinstaller/dist/notolog directly. No Debian
patch series is applied. To discard source-package changes, extract the .dsc
again into a new directory with `dpkg-source -x`.

For a new upstream version, update debian/changelog and release metadata,
replace src/ with the matching upstream release, rebuild the executable, and
regenerate the source package.
